PARITY & ACCEPTANCE
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Data sources (web → native, no HTTP in the view):
  • useTranslation     → NewVersionBannerStrings facade (P1/S10), NSLocalizedString table.
  • useVersionWatcher  → NewVersionBannerSource (P1/S8): PollingNewVersionBannerSource probes
                         /system/version through an injected VersionProbe (host wires its API client),
                         captures the boot baseline, re-polls every 5 min, derives latest != boot.

States — every one renders (no hidden surface):
  loading (boot probe) · empty (up-to-date OR dismissed-for-current — friendly card, never a blank box) ·
  error (boot probe failed; web swallows to null, surfaced here) · available (Sparkles banner +
  Later/Reload) · stale + offline freshness chip (poll failed w/ cached version; one-shot auto-refresh
  on the stale transition).

Web-source-specific branches reproduced exactly:
  • newVersionAvailable rule (boot && latest && latest !== boot).
  • per-version dismissal (web sessionStorage `teslasync:new-version-dismissed-for`) → in-memory,
    app-session-scoped store (faithful sessionStorage parity: resets on relaunch, nudges a stale
    session on cold start).
  • reset-on-new-version (web useEffect clearing a dismissal once the deploy advances past it).
  • handleReload (window.location.reload) → host-wired onReload seam (a native app updates via the
    App Store; the host chooses re-bootstrap / reload-embedded-web / update-flow). Reload + Later always
    render (web always offers both).

i18n keys: 3 web keys present + resolved via the facade (no English literals in Swift):
  app.newVersion.message = "A new version of TeslaSync is available."
  app.newVersion.later   = "Later"
  app.newVersion.reload  = "Reload"
  + 11 native P4-leaf/a11y keys (loadingA11y, upToDateTitle/Message, errorTitle, retry,
  versionDetailA11y, live, stale, offline, staleA11y, offlineA11y).
  Dead web keys: 0. Missing web keys: 0.

Accessibility: banner is one spoken status element (web role="status" aria-live) with the message +
target version as its label; Later/Reload are individually-focusable TSButtons with explicit labels;
Sparkles glyph + chevron decorative; freshness chip is a labelled refresh button. Dynamic Type via
tokens; reduce-motion respected via TSFadeIn.

